WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.255 --> 00:00:07.630
KRISH SRINIVASAN:
Good afternoon.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.030
I'm Krish Srinivasan.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.120
I head the Cloud and Compute
Organization at Target.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.360
For those who shop at Target
and for those who love shopping

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.230
at Target, I'm sure you
know that we are all

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.940
about inspiration and joy.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.600
And for those who don't
know about Target,

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.540
we are one of the biggest
retailers in the US,

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.850
across 50 states.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.520
And I have a simple proposition
that I want to start with.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.800
Any organization that wants
to serve its customers

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.230
or is thinking about
customer satisfaction

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.300
has to think about
inspiration and joy.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.320
Now how many of us
from an IT standpoint

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.110
think inspiration and joy?

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.960
At Target, we do.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.080
Technology has been a key
factor behind Target's growth

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.250
over the last few years.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.280
And we are just getting started.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.400
See it's even more critical
because if your goal is

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.220
to be America's
easiest place to shop,

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.220
technology becomes a
foundational stone for us.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.350
Now having said that,
we know that our guests

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.240
have high expectations.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.460
They want us to do well.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.700
They believe in us.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.820
They're rooting for us.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.920
They want us to innovate.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.710
And simply, they just
want us to be Target.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.390
So with all these
high expectations,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.200
how do we look up and out
from a technology standpoint?

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.470
How do we make sure that we
build the right platforms

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.380
and capabilities from an
infrastructure standpoint,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:45.350
so that we are ready for a
future guest when they come up

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.570
with those new experiences,
or when they're looking

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.070
for those new experiences?

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.060
And that's what I'm going
to talk about today.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.070
Last year our CIO Mike McNamara
was at this very event.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.700
And he shared the business
strategy and the technology

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.910
transformation at Target.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:09.139
As Mike stated, our
strategy is indeed working.

00:02:09.139 --> 00:02:10.855
And cloud is an enabler.

00:02:10.855 --> 00:02:12.230
And thank you to
Google for being

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.890
part of the journey as well.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.340
In fact, this is our
fifth straight year

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:20.250
where we are growing
25% year over year.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.170
And I'm happy to say that last
year was the first year where

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.890
we ran 100% of our
Cloud Commerce workload

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.540
on Google Cloud Platform.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.690
So Google, thank you
for a flawless holiday

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.250
season in 2018.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.980
Together, we came together,
and we provided our guests

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.830
some phenomenal experiences.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:41.270
Now what you see
in the screen is

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:44.060
these are industry leading
fulfillment services

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.170
for our guest.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:49.320
And we're just adding
on more and more to it.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.070
Couple of examples,
let's say you're at work,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.060
and you want to make that order.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.800
You are looking for something.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.750
But you don't have the
patience to wait for two days.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.420
You have the capability
now to make that order

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.920
online from your work and pick
it up on your way back home.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.760
What about this?

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.210
A busy mom, it's raining.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:16.320
She has two little ones,
little ones in her backseat.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.370
And one of them is starting
to throw some tantrums.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.810
The other one's begin--

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.920
starts to begin to meltdown.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.130
And I know some of
us have been there.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.530
She does not have to
get out of her car.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.100
And what we have done is we have
given that mom the capability

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.970
to punch in that order,
and when she drives

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.820
her car to the parking
lot, our team members

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.820
get notified through a
geo-location service.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.850
And within two minutes,
our store team members

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.632
will come and place the
order in the car trunk.

00:03:48.632 --> 00:03:50.340
And these are the
experiences that we are

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.630
talking about in the future.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.815
Now how did we get here?

00:03:54.815 --> 00:03:56.940
I would say there are three
foundational principles

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.350
at Target we believe in.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:02.490
First, technology has to
be experience focused.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.590
Now what do I mean by that?

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:11.970
At Target, experiences takes
first before technology does.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.019
All of us have been an incident,
outages and operational cause.

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:18.149
Something happens,
we get on a call.

00:04:18.149 --> 00:04:21.000
And this is where typical
IT organization do,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.170
there is a server failure.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.295
There's a database failure.

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:25.560
Or some software
developer over there

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.330
did a full table
scan, brought out--

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.630
brought down an application.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.220
At Target, we look at it
a little bit different.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.950
When we have an outage or
an incident at Target, yes,

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.750
all of us do get on the call.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.990
But the first question
we ask is, what

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.860
is the impact to the guest?

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.870
What is the impact
to the team member?

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:44.560
We understand that very clearly.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.430
And then we talk about, what
is the technical or technology

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.300
issues?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:55.800
Second, architecture must be
simple, elegant, and adaptive.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.470
And what I mean by that is
when we write applications

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.300
at Target, we want
to make sure that we

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.760
don't have a vendor lock-in.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.040
and there is this
foundational principle

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.010
that platforms are the path to
the future and not just tools.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.610
And the third thing
I would say is,

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.730
technology has to embrace
cloud and open source, which

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.590
is why we went with Google.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.430
Now we all know
that cloud gives us

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.370
the speed and agility
and elasticity and all

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.640
that good stuff.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.700
But what about open source?

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.620
At Target, when we
have a solution,

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.730
and we're looking for a
solution for a problem,

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.188
the first thing we
do is internally

00:05:29.188 --> 00:05:31.590
look inside and see whether
we can repurpose a solution

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.900
that we already have.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.920
If for some reason
that's not available,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.230
we then go to the
open-source community.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.040
And we look at it.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.170
And if for some reason
that's not available,

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.450
we then go ahead and
write it on our own,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.580
even before we go
to the vendors.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.620
And the best part
is, once we write it,

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.520
we contribute back to the
open-source community.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:54.212
So I talked about these
high expectations earlier

00:05:54.212 --> 00:05:55.170
that guests have in us.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.100
They want us to do well.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.210
They want us to be Target.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.550
They want us to innovate.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.470
This is where the next
chapter of innovation

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.200
comes in that I talked
about earlier, which

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.410
is all about focusing on our
guest and our team members

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.280
in the future.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:11.820
Be it a quart of milk, or
that beautiful rug you're

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:16.740
looking at, or that perfect
gift that you want for somebody,

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:20.610
Target is a positive force
behind millions of people

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:24.100
in the US every single day.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.510
Now we have about 30 million of
our guests shop at our stores

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:31.260
every month, about 100 million
visits in our digital fronts.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:36.300
So to do this, we operate
in at about 1,850 stores.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.510
We have 29-- or 39
distribution centers.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.000
We have our own
two data centers.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.820
And yes, we also have
Google Cloud as well.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:48.010
But-- and here's the
challenge that comes in--

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:52.360
what if-- what if all
these assets came together

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:52.943
seamlessly?

00:06:52.943 --> 00:06:54.610
What if I could take
a workload and just

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.050
deploy it across the board?

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:04.010
And what if I don't look at
these 1850 stores as stores,

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:07.920
but I look at them as yet
another extension of my cloud.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.040
So tomorrow, I'm not
going to have just GCP.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.190
I may have 1,850
cloud environments,

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.270
just think about that
power, and the capability,

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.770
and the scalability
that we can get.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:23.250
And what if there
is a scenario where

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.110
I have five stores in New York,
three stores in San Francisco,

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.690
I want to do two
pilots the same day.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.850
I get the results back.

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.160
And I pick one of them,
because one has a better

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.020
experience for a guest.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.630
And within a few hours,
what if I can just

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:44.250
deploy to 1,850 stores across
the hundreds of thousands

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.950
of devices that are
running in those stores?

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:50.580
We have close to 130,000
Android mobile devices that

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.870
are running in those stores.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.360
And what if I can
do that seamlessly?

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.410
And here's the best part,
what if I could do everything

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.290
that I said and still
make the underlying

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.650
infrastructure completely
invisible to our engineers?

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.200
So they are focused on
what they're good at, which

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:10.260
is to write great software
that can delight our guests

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.975
and make our team members happy.

00:08:11.975 --> 00:08:14.350
They don't have to worry about
the underlying technology.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:17.130
They don't have to worry about
patches, the version upgrades.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.630
We take care of all of that.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:21.990
And that's what we have
been working on at Target.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.230
Our engineers have been hard
at work for the last 18 months,

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:28.050
building this platform at Target
to solve this exact challenge

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.400
for the future.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.190
Within Target we call
it as TAP, or T-A-P,

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.850
which stands for Target
Application Platform.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:40.570
The mission of this
platform is very simple.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.990
It's to make Target the best
place to write and deliver

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:48.330
software with zero
touch infrastructure.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.560
So in closing, I want to go
back to my initial proposition

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.720
that I made, that
any organization that

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.380
wants to provide
great customer service

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.430
must focus on
inspiration and joy.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.790
Our guests get
inspiration and joy

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:07.190
from our products and
services, which they love.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.440
And they're rooting for us.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.230
Our store team members
get inspiration and joy

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:15.870
by delivering those
services to our guests.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:18.020
Our technology team members
get inspiration and joy

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:22.130
by building and innovating for
the next set of experiences.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.650
And that's the thing
about inspiration and joy,

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:29.370
when it's going great, you get
to renew it every single day.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:30.710
And that's what we do at Target.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.668
And we are just getting started.

00:09:32.668 --> 00:09:34.460
Thank you, and have a
wonderful conference.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:38.410
[MUSIC PLAYING]

